    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0276" n="246" xml:id="pg246"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.AA/7–1447: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-14T20:00:00+02:00">July 14, 1947—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3850. British hope to keep situation in respect of membership applications UN on
                    fluid basis and have instructed Cadogan to make no irrevocable commitment re any
                    applicant. What British fear, according to Jebb, is commitment which might be
                    made subsequently embarrassing by intervening “atrocity” of applicant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
